20:{"_type":"https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1","subject":[{"name":"C12","digest":{"sha256":"0f100e48845e38678f82c3b57cf9f0d9532963ffa8aa2cefe0e94f9a561237fb"}}],"predicateType":"https://github.com/lonic-software/tetel/captured-fact/v1","predicate":{"verdict":"qualifies","pass":"068c02e043beda16","reported_kind":"run","source":"proc:workspace-068c02e043beda16","extent":["proc: grep -n -e NON_COVERAGE -e coverage it never claimed -e never declared themselves -e uncensused -e unverifiable /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/checks.rs /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/report.rs /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/main.rs /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/mcp.rs (exit 0)","/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/report.rs lines 1-120","/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/report.rs lines 240-296","/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/checks.rs lines 1220-1310"],"world":[{"root":"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel","state":"git:5076b5fe177f2ab87259d8d1e36881c055e0be35001992b01789e8ac000461a8"}],"note":"The mechanism claims check out: NON_COVERAGE exists in report.rs, its comment says verbatim \"a refusal that fired is easily read as coverage it never claimed\", its existing last entry is the exact analogue of proposed entry (a), and the insincere-examination ceiling is registered in scope.rs as \"the limit this project registered as permanently out of reach\" (F5). What I could not establish is the parenthetical resting on the ticket — \"deciding what counts as a premise is design judgment (the ticket says so)\": the ticket lives in the planning repository, which is outside this pass's bound, so that attribution stands ungraded rather than confirmed.","pin":"sha256:263d79c809e61c0d040df5b932fec45bedd444843c9aa31e727ee288e941a7f9","timestamp":1786174487}}
