umes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/ledger.rs lines 80-135"],"world":[{"root":"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel","state":"git:ba3b5ed2df92b4e7b935e78719bc9e45d644b1bd061a444651033cc3e9b24719"}],"note":"Right in substance, wrong in one clause. The clause \"beside `notes_outside_extent` and `mint_windows`, which is where every snapshot-dependent finding is already computed\" is false as written. `check_file` has exactly one `if snapshot_dir.is_dir()` block and it computes `notes_outside_extent`, `tree_states`/`tree_ungradable`, `uncensused_targets`, `unquoted_premises` and `mint_windows` — but two snapshot-dependent findings are computed outside it: `findings.provenance = snapshot::check(path, &source)`, and `findings.grounding_provenance`, whose authoring identity comes from `workspace::identity_of(&snapshot_dir)` and which distinguishes NoSnapshot from SnapshotWithoutIdentity. `unverifiable_targets` and `unverifiable_transplants` are likewise computed in the complementary `if !snapshot_dir.is_dir()` branch. The narrower statement — that the block is where every snapshot-dependent finding that requires reading the snapshot's logs is computed — would have been true. Everything else in the claim checks out: `prose::load_all` does discard timestamps so prose.jsonl must be read directly; `check_file` does already hold `ledger.claims` (imported from the rendered document) and `evidence_records`; the digest argument is exact, since both `build_statement` and `record_from_fact` compute sha256 over the ledger-derived `claim.proposition`, `compose::ledger_cell` replaces newlines with spaces, and `ledger::split_row_cells` trims every cell at both push sites, so a proposition with an embedded newline or edge whitespace hashes differently from the claims.jsonl string; `machine_check_failed` is a fixed OR over ten named lists plus provenance and adding a field does not touch it; and without a snapshot the list would be silently uncomputed exactly as `notes_outside_extent` and `mint_windows` are.","pin":"sha256:137800720ce83837f990e86ff3238128e2478e333f602eff120eb2186ad92512","timestamp":1786195052}}
78:{"_type":"https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1","subject":[{"name":"C13","digest":{"sha256":"68cccfadd0c968048241f0db0b69d05a3765abc36298dfff450f0f3463d0f94a"}}],"predicateType":"https://github.com/lonic-software/tetel/captured-fact/v1","predicate":{"verdict":"qualifies","pass":"91c4b0f5060af639","reported_kind":"run","source":"proc:workspace-91c4b0f5060af639","extent":["proc: python3 -c import os\nroot='/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel'\nskip_names=('tet30-prose-revised-since-grounding.md','tet30-prose-revised-since-grounding.md.evidence.jsonl')\npats=['render','NON_COVERAGE','Findings','check_file','prose_after_proof','block_offsets']\ndef walk(exclude_git_target):\n    files=[]\n    for dp,dns,fns in os.walk(root):\n        rel=os.path.relpath(dp,root)\n        parts=rel.split(os.sep)\n        if 'tet30-prose-revised-since-grounding.md.tetel' in parts: continue\n        if exclude_git_target and (parts[0]=='.git' or parts[0]=='target'): continue\n        for f in fns:\n            if f in skip_names: continue\n            files.append(os.path.join(dp,f))\n    return files\nfor ex in (False,True):\n    files=walk(ex)\n    res={p:[0,0,0] for p in pats}\n    nb=0\n    for fp in files:\n        try: data=open(fp,'rb').read()\n        except OSError: continue\n        if b'\\x00' in data: continue\n        nb+=1\n        for line in data.split(b'\\n'):\n            for p in pats:\n                if p.encode() in line:\n                    r=res[p]; r[0]+=1; r[1]+=len(line); r[2]+=len(line)+1\n    print('exclude_git_target=',ex,'files scanned',nb)\n    for p in pats: print('   ',p,'lines',res[p][0],'bytes(no nl)',res[p][1],'bytes(+nl)',res[p][2])\n (exit 0)","proc: python3 -c import os\nfor m in ['tet28-modification-target-census.md','tet29-imported-mechanism-premises.md']:\n    d='/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/docs/design/'+m+'.tetel'\n    best=(0,None)\n    for f in sorted(os.listdir(d)):\n        p=os.path.join(d,f)\n        mx=max((len(l) for l in open(p,'rb').read().split(b'\\n')), default=0)\n        print(m,f,'longest line',mx)\n        if mx>best[0]: best=(mx,f)\n    print(m,'=> longest overall',best)\n (exit 0)","proc: grep -n worktree\\|census\\|root /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/targets.rs (exit 0)"],"world":[{"root":"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel","state":"git:ba3b5ed2df92b4e7b935e78719bc9e45d644b1bd061a444651033cc3e9b24719"}],"note":"Every figure I could reproduce reproduced exactly, but two parts of the claim I could not establish at all, because they are properties of this memo's own evidence log and snapshot — which an independent grounding pass must not open. Reproduced: `render` 486 lines / 373271 bytes over the non-binary files of this tree with this memo's own artifacts excluded, and 447 / 311672 with `.git/` and `target/` excluded as well; `NON_COVERAGE` 35 / 95637; `Findings` 23 / 57418; `check_file` 5 / 285; `prose_after_proof` and `block_offsets` nothing at all. Also reproduced: tet29's longest snapshot line is 57249 bytes and tet28's is 34477, both in facts.jsonl, both whole-file dumps on one JSON line. The ordering the claim ends on holds on those numbers. Not established: the opening sentence \"took six whole-worktree searches\", which would require reading this memo's own targets.jsonl; and the entire \"Time\" paragraph (529/1136689, 550/1202134, 59 records / 164392 bytes, a 574898-byte fact line), which describes this memo's own evidence log and snapshot mid-review. The claim itself says those figures do not hold still, so this is a qualification about what an independent pass can witness, not a challenge to them.","pin":"sha256:70a36335add20155599c10873891078cac14c11a5abda1557bf19f7f30bcd44e","timestamp":1786195058}}
