125:{"_type":"https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1","subject":[{"name":"C13","digest":{"sha256":"ef5d3c2852ffc7fe4b27faf7acbac77c714de80eab02a652e9915f38d04078cd"}}],"predicateType":"https://github.com/lonic-software/tetel/captured-fact/v1","predicate":{"verdict":"qualifies","pass":"43e097204af22bea","reported_kind":"run","source":"proc:workspace-43e097204af22bea","extent":["proc: python3 -c import os\nR='/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel'\nSK={'tet30-prose-revised-since-grounding.md','tet30-prose-revised-since-grounding.md.evidence.jsonl'}\ndef scan(symbols,excl_git_target,excl_tet30):\n    res={s:[0,0] for s in symbols}\n    for dp,dn,fn in os.walk(R):\n        rel=os.path.relpath(dp,R)\n        if excl_git_target:\n            dn[:]=[d for d in dn if not (rel=='.' and d in ('.git','target'))]\n        if excl_tet30 and 'tet30-prose-revised-since-grounding.md.tetel' in dp: continue\n        for f in fn:\n            if excl_tet30 and f in SK: continue\n            p=os.path.join(dp,f)\n            try: data=open(p,'rb').read()\n            except Exception: continue\n            if b'\\x00' in data: continue\n            for line in data.split(b'\\n'):\n                for s in symbols:\n                    if s.encode() in line:\n                        res[s][0]+=1;res[s][1]+=len(line)\n    return res\nsy=['render','NON_COVERAGE','Findings','check_file','prose_after_proof','block_offsets']\nprint('with .git+target, tet30 artifacts excluded:',scan(sy,False,True))\nprint('without .git+target, tet30 excluded:      ',scan(sy,True,True))\n (exit 0)","proc: python3 -c import os,json\nD='/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/docs/design/'\nfor m in ('tet28-modification-target-census.md','tet29-imported-mechanism-premises.md'):\n    p=D+m+'.tetel/facts.jsonl'\n    lines=open(p,'rb').read().split(b'\\n')\n    mx=max(lines,key=len)\n    print(m,'longest facts.jsonl line',len(mx),'bytes; total lines',len([l for l in lines if l.strip()]))\n    j=json.loads(mx)\n    ex=j.get('Create',j).get('extent') if isinstance(j,dict) else None\n    print('   event',j.get('event'),'id',j.get('id'),'extent labels',[e.get('label') for e in (j.get('extent') or [])][:4])\nR='/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel'\ndef scan(sym,root):\n    n=b=0\n    for dp,dn,fn in os.walk(root):\n        if 'tet30-prose' in dp: continue\n        for f in fn:\n            if 'tet30-prose' in f: continue\n            try: data=open(os.path.join(dp,f),'rb').read()\n            except Exception: continue\n            if b'\\x00' in data: continue\n            for line in data.split(b'\\n'):\n                if sym.encode() in line: n+=1;b+=len(line)\n    return n,b\nfor s in ('render','NON_COVERAGE','Findings','check_file','prose_after_proof'):\n    print(s,'whole docs/design/ contributes',scan(s,R+'/docs/design'),' src/ contributes',scan(s,R+'/src'))\n (exit 0)","proc: grep -n census\\|whole-worktree\\|worktree\\|root /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/targets.rs (exit 0)"],"world":[{"root":"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel","state":"git:ba3b5ed2df92b4e7b935e78719bc9e45d644b1bd061a444651033cc3e9b24719"}],"note":"Every figure I can reach reproduces to the byte: render 486/373271 and 447/311672 without .git and target, NON_COVERAGE 35/95637, Findings 23/57418, check_file 5/285, nothing for the two green-field symbols, and the two snapshot line lengths 57249 (tet29) and 34477 (tet28), both whole-file dumps on one JSON line. The ordering and direction hold and are large: docs/design/ alone contributes 284701 of render's 373271 bytes and 95575 of NON_COVERAGE's 95637, against src/'s 15802 and 62, and a discussed symbol costs about 1300x an undiscussed one. What I cannot witness is what the claim itself says cannot be witnessed: the count of six whole-worktree searches, and the time-varying measurements (529/1136689 then 550/1202134, 59 records / 164392 bytes, a 574898-byte snapshot fact line). All of those range over this memo's own targets log, evidence log and snapshot, which an independent pass must not open. So the claim is graded as: reproducible half exact, self-referential half unreachable by construction.","pin":"sha256:9868f1833fb044d0909f7532d34b35fedca49721ca0f930d59ed0f0e97087982","timestamp":1786197694}}
12:{"event":"Create","id":"C11","prop":"The implementation surface is six declared modification targets and nothing else: one new field on `Findings`; one new function `prose_after_proof` computing the list from the snapshot's `prose.jsonl` and `claims.jsonl` plus the evidence records `check_file` has already loaded; one call to it inside `check_file`'s existing `if snapshot_dir.is_dir()` block, beside `notes_outside_extent` and `mint_windows`, which is where every snapshot-dependent finding is already computed; one `block_offsets` function in `compose` consumed by `render`; one print loop and one added clause in the human-owed scope sentence in `report::render`; and new entries in `NON_COVERAGE`. `machine_check_failed` is not touched, which is what makes this human-owed by construction rather than by intention. Nothing new ships in the snapshot — `prose.jsonl` and `claims.jsonl` are already in `SNAPSHOT_FILES` — no schema changes, no command is executed and no file the document names is opened, so `check`'s standing guarantees are unaffected. Without a snapshot the list is simply not computed, silently, exactly as `notes_outside_extent` and `mint_windows` are not, and the existing missing-snapshot bullet already tells the reader why. Four things belong in `NON_COVERAGE`: false prose that ships alongside a claim revision, which the ticket concedes and this design does not fix; a paragraph that cites nothing, which has no edge to compare against; whether the two clocks behind the ordering agree; and whether the prose is wrong at all, which nothing here judges.","from":["F5","F2","F12","F13"],"timestamp":1786190048}
15:{"event":"Create","id":"C13","prop":"Declaring this design's own modification targets measured a cost of the census mechanism that compounds with each memo the repository accumulates, and it is worth recording where the next ticket in this family will see it. A census is a whole-worktree search whose entire output is captured into a fact and shipped in the snapshot; in this repository the two previous memos' snapshots hold whole file dumps on single JSON lines, up to 57110 bytes each, so a search for a symbol this crate discusses re-captures those dumps. The measured weight for the four symbols this design must modify that already exist: `render` 486 matching lines and 405019 characters, `NON_COVERAGE` 35 lines and 98828 characters, `Findings` 23 lines and 59.2 KB, `check_file` 5 lines and 285 bytes. Two consequences follow. The captures exceeded what the authoring surface would return, so the symbol population was established by the search while its individual sites went unread by the author — the census establishes rooting and extent, never that anyone looked at each site, which is a thing the census's own printed non-coverage already says in a different form. And the cost grows: every memo added to `docs/design/` enlarges the next memo's census of any symbol it discusses.","from":["F11","F13","F12"],"timestamp":1786190138}
16:{"event":"Revise","id":"C13","prop":"Declaring this design's own modification targets took six whole-worktree searches — `check_file`, `prose_after_proof` and `block_offsets` in one fact, `Findings`, `NON_COVERAGE` and `render` in another — and measured a cost of the census mechanism that compounds with each memo the repository accumulates. A census is a whole-worktree search whose entire output is captured into a fact and shipped in the snapshot; in this repository the two previous memos' snapshots hold whole file dumps on single JSON lines, up to 57110 bytes each, so a search for a symbol this crate discusses re-captures those dumps. The measured weight for the four of the six symbols that already exist: `render` 486 matching lines and 405019 characters, `NON_COVERAGE` 35 lines and 98828 characters, `Findings` 23 lines and 59.2 KB, `check_file` 5 lines and 285 bytes; the two green-field symbols have no occurrences at all and are censused by the searches that established that. Two consequences follow. The largest captures exceeded what the authoring surface would return, so those symbol populations were established by the search while their individual sites went unread by the author — the census establishes rooting and extent, never that anyone looked at each site, which is a thing the census's own printed non-coverage already says in a different form. And the cost grows: every memo added to `docs/design/` enlarges the next memo's census of any symbol it discusses.","from":null,"why":"Review paired this claim against P20, which asserts that six targets required six whole-worktree searches. The count is in the cited facts — F12 records three searches (check_file, prose_after_proof, block_offsets) and F13 three more (Findings, NON_COVERAGE, render) — but the proposition did not carry it, leaving the paragraph asserting something no claim stated. Adding the count rather than weakening the paragraph.","timestamp":1786190228}
