an leaving claims about it to rest on an extent the note never mentioned.\",\"timestamp\":1786131172}\n104:| F7 | The assembly-and-verification surfaces TET-29 extends, first-hand. compose.rs: render appends render_targets between the prose and the evidence ledger; the section renders \"None declared...\" once any claim exists (\"the hole is the finding\" — \"an absent section would make the same omission invisible, which is the failure mode, not the fix\"); withdrawn targets are dropped, live ones render as a two-column table \\|`symbol`\\|F#\\|; only labels are rendered, never absolute keys (\"a committed document should not carry /Users/<someone>/...\"), and captured output is deliberately NOT rendered into the document (\"unbounded ... it is in the snapshot for anyone who needs it, and a document that inlined it would bury the prose\"). checks.rs: Findings has uncensused_targets as a MACHINE failure (\"re-verified against the shipped snapshot ... what this catches is the document that never passed through that verb: hand-authored, edited after rendering, or carrying a target row its own snapshot does not have. Both directions are checked\"), and unverifiable_targets as human-owed when no snapshot shipped; machine_check_failed() ORs grammar/subset/abutting/unsettled/cascade/ledger/verdict-disagreement/out-of-proof/uncensused-targets/provenance; out_of_proof (every record grades a wording the claim no longer carries) is a machine failure whose remedy is reproving. report.rs: exit codes 0/1/2; NON_COVERAGE is a const list printed item by item (\"tetel does not catch: ...\"), and TET-28 added five census entries to it with a comment explaining why (\"a refusal that fired is easily read as coverage it never claimed\"); first entry is \"dependents that never declared themselves\". | /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/compose.rs lines 1-130; /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/checks.rs lines 120-215; /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/report.rs lines 13-40 