tanding choice as every other snapshot-dependent finding\\\". facts.jsonl ships in SNAPSHOT_FILES with full outputs, so byte-for-byte containment re-checking needs no execution. The claim itself flags the render/--out asymmetry as new and most debatable, which is accurate — nothing shipped refuses at --out today.\",\"pin\":\"sha256:0a7fd36de509936ec5d5cb4e1bc0286b9c19842c50dd8385a9c99d06a01763dc\",\"timestamp\":1786175433}}\n41:{\"_type\":\"https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1\",\"subject\":[{\"name\":\"C11\",\"digest\":{\"sha256\":\"f9542ddd33f0b55ed2e6421d8e9b730f6526506f234a3b8f208fec6dc7c04bfd\"}}],\"predicateType\":\"https://github.com/lonic-software/tetel/captured-fact/v1\",\"predicate\":{\"verdict\":\"supports\",\"pass\":\"c7ccb4bc34bdb0bf\",\"reported_kind\":\"run\",\"source\":\"proc:workspace-c7ccb4bc34bdb0bf\",\"extent\":[\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/compose.rs\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/snapshot.rs\",\"no-match: --out in /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/main.rs\",\"no-match: NON_COVERAGE in /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/checks.rs\",\"no-match: never declared themselves in /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/checks.rs\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/checks.rs (grep: uncensused)\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/report.rs (grep: NON_COVERAGE)\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/report.rs (grep: declared themselves)\",\"no-match: out_path in /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/report.rs lines 1-60\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/main.rs (grep: render)\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/main.rs lines 232-268\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/main.rs lines 700-745\",\"no-match: runs nothing in /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/checks.rs\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/checks.rs (grep: unverifiable)\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/checks.rs lines 1220-1310\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/checks.rs lines 130-215\"],\"world\":[{\"root\":\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel\",\"state\":\"git:5076b5fe177f2ab87259d8d1e36881c055e0be35001992b01789e8ac000461a8\"}],\"note\":\"The conventions the section claims to follow are compose.rs's shipped ones: render_targets renders once any claim exists, as \\\"None declared...\\\" when empty, because \\\"the hole is the finding\\\"; withdrawn records are dropped; render_facts renders labels and never absolute keys, for exactly the committed-document reason; and captured output is deliberately not inlined because \\\"It is unbounded (a `run` can capture megabytes)\\\" — so the claimed difference (an author-bounded premise selection is safe to inline) is a genuine, correctly characterised departure rather than a contradiction. The fenced-block rationale is also grounded: ledger_cell must replace embedded newlines because a markdown table row is one physical line, which would break byte-fidelity for multi-line premises.\",\"pin\":\"sha256:0a7fd36de509936ec5d5cb4e1bc0286b9c19842c50dd8385a9c99d06a01763dc\",\"timestamp\":1786175455}}\n42:{\"_type\":\"https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1\",\"subject\":[{\"name\":\"C12\",\"digest\":{\"sha256\":\"d637582afecb0322e77e93eeea329f08ff98654395270d44339f623056a3c894\"}}],\"predicateType\":\"https://github.com/lonic-software/tetel/captured-fact/v1\",\"predicate\":{\"verdict\":\"supports\",\"pass\":\"c7ccb4bc34bdb0bf\",\"reported_kind\":\"run\",\"source\":\"proc:workspace-c7ccb4bc34bdb0bf\",\"extent\":[\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/compose.rs\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/snapshot.rs\",\"no-match: --out in /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/main.rs\",\"no-match: NON_COVERAGE in /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/checks.rs\",\"no-match: never declared themselves in /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/checks.rs\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/checks.rs (grep: uncensused)\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/report.rs (grep: NON_COVERAGE)\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/report.rs (grep: declared themselves)\",\"no-match: out_path in /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/report.rs lines 1-60\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/main.rs (grep: render)\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/main.rs lines 232-268\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/main.rs lines 700-745\",\"no-match: runs nothing in /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/checks.rs\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/checks.rs (grep: unverifiable)\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/checks.rs lines 1220-1310\",\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/checks.rs lines 130-215\"],\"world\":[{\"root\":\"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel\",\"state\":\"git:5076b5fe177f2ab87259d8d1e36881c055e0be35001992b01789e8ac000461a8\"}],\"note\":\"The list and its purpose are real: report.rs's NON_COVERAGE is a printed const whose census block carries the quoted rationale verbatim (\\\"a refusal that fired is easily read as coverage it never claimed\\\"), and entry (a) mirrors the shipped target entry (\\\"a modification target the author never declared — no refusal can reach it, and the empty section is its only trace\\\"). Each of the six proposed entries names something that is genuinely outside a format-level check of byte containment — selection breadth, discharge-to-premise linkage, and donor truth are all content. The ticket-stipulation clause is recorded as the ticket's stipulation, which I did not and could not re-establish from source.\",\"pin\":\"sha256:0a7fd36de509936ec5d5cb4e1bc0286b9c19842c50dd8385a9c99d06a01763dc\",\"timestamp\":1786175464}}\n44:{\"_type\":\"https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1\",\"subject\":[{\"name\":\"C13\",\"digest\":{\"sha256\":\"412d6f2d99d275ca08a4e240cf883e381b0442269b9bead431d537db979b6589\"}}],\"predicateType\":\"https://github.com/lonic-software/tetel/captured-fact/v1\",\"predicate\":{\"verdict\":\"supports\",\"pass\":\"c7ccb4bc34