18:{"event":"Create","id":"F15","note":"How sensitive a census figure is to scope and to when it is taken, measured over the same worktree four ways per symbol (counting matching lines and their raw byte length across every non-binary file, with .git/ and target/ either included or skipped, and this memo's own tet30 artifacts either included or skipped).\n\n`render`: 529 lines / 1136689 bytes with everything; 486 / 373271 excluding tet30 only; 490 / 1075090 excluding .git+target only; 447 / 311672 excluding both.\n`NON_COVERAGE`: 54 / 737911 with everything; 35 / 95637 excluding tet30; unchanged by excluding .git+target.\n`Findings`: 41 / 698345 with everything; 23 / 57418 excluding tet30; unchanged by excluding .git+target.\n\nTwo things this settles. The earlier figures recorded in this workspace (render 486 lines / 373271 bytes, NON_COVERAGE 35 / 95637, Findings 23 / 57418) are reproduced exactly by the \"excluding tet30 only\" column, which is what the tree looked like when they were taken — before this memo and its snapshot existed. And the same symbol in the same tree yields 447, 486, 490 or 529 matching lines and 311672 to 1136689 bytes depending only on which directories are in scope and whether this memo's own artifacts are yet on disk. So a census byte figure is a property of an instrument and a moment, not of the symbol; the ordering — that `render` is far larger than `check_file`'s 5 lines — is what survives across all four scopings.","extent":[{"key":"/usr/bin/python3 -c import os\nroot='/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel'\ndef count(sym,skip_vcs,skip_tet30):\n    n=0;tot=0\n    for dp,dirs,files in os.walk(root):\n        rel=os.path.relpath(dp,root)\n        if skip_vcs and (rel=='.git' or rel.startswith('.git'+os.sep) or rel=='target' or rel.startswith('target'+os.sep)): continue\n        for f in files:\n            if skip_tet30 and 'tet30' in os.path.join(rel,f): continue\n            try: d=open(os.path.join(dp,f),'rb').read()\n            except Exception: continue\n            if b'\\x00' in d[:8192]: continue\n            for line in d.split(b'\\n'):\n                if sym.encode() in line: n+=1; tot+=len(line)\n    return n,tot\nfor sym in ['render','NON_COVERAGE','Findings']:\n    for sv in (False,True):\n        for st in (False,True):\n            n,t=count(sym,sv,st)\n            print('%-13s skip_vcs+target=%-5s skip_tet30=%-5s -> %4d lines %8d bytes'%(sym,sv,st,n,t))\n","label":"proc: /usr/bin/python3 -c import os\nroot='/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel'\ndef count(sym,skip_vcs,skip_tet30):\n    n=0;tot=0\n    for dp,dirs,files in os.walk(root):\n        rel=os.path.relpath(dp,root)\n        if skip_vcs and (rel=='.git' or rel.startswith('.git'+os.sep) or rel=='target' or rel.startswith('target'+os.sep)): continue\n        for f in files:\n            if skip_tet30 and 'tet30' in os.path.join(rel,f): continue\n            try: d=open(os.path.join(dp,f),'rb').read()\n            except Exception: continue\n            if b'\\x00' in d[:8192]: continue\n            for line in d.split(b'\\n'):\n                if sym.encode() in line: n+=1; tot+=len(line)\n    return n,tot\nfor sym in ['render','NON_COVERAGE','Findings']:\n    for sv in (False,True):\n        for st in (False,True):\n            n,t=count(sym,sv,st)\n            print('%-13s skip_vcs+target=%-5s skip_tet30=%-5s -> %4d lines %8d bytes'%(sym,sv,st,n,t))\n (exit 0)","world_root":"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel","world_state":"git:ba3b5ed2df92b4e7b935e78719bc9e45d644b1bd061a444651033cc3e9b24719","kind":"Proc","pattern":"","out_len":984}],"output":"render        skip_vcs+target=False skip_tet30=False ->  529 lines  1136689 bytes\nrender        skip_vcs+target=False skip_tet30=True  ->  486 lines   373271 bytes\nrender        skip_vcs+target=True  skip_tet30=False ->  490 lines  1075090 bytes\nrender        skip_vcs+target=True  skip_tet30=True  ->  447 lines   311672 bytes\nNON_COVERAGE  skip_vcs+target=False skip_tet30=False ->  